<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siga was an ancient city near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tafna">Tafna</a> river in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, the capital of the Masaesylian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syphax">Syphax</a> in the late 3rd century BCE. A Punic trading post, it later became a Roman town. Nearby at Beni Rhenane stands a royal mausoleum attributed to Syphax's dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siga.jpg" alt="Siga" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Faycal.09 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siga,_general_view_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
